s of family members after a suicide</article-title><source>J Fam Pract</source><year>1991</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>375</fpage><lpage>380</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1919454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Garner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The case against "the evidence": a different perspective on evidence-based medicine</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><year>2002</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11772844</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1192/bjp.180.1.8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Fan</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lohan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bereaved parents' outcomes 4 to 60 months after their children's deaths by accident, suicide, or homicide: a comparative study demonstrating differences</article-title><source>Death Stud</source><year>2003</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12508827</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/07481180302871</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>